    summary_en: "The open-source AI Agent control platform Paperclip has been found to contain several severe vulnerabilities. The highest severity vulnerability, CVE-2026-41679 (CVSS 10.0), stems from flaws in open registration and permission checks. Unauthorized attackers can register accounts, approve CLI credentials, and exploit the company's import API to bypass administrator privileges, thereby deploying a malicious instruction-containing .paperclip.yaml configuration file and achieving arbitrary command execution on the server side. Another vulnerability, GHSA-x8hx-rhr2-9rf7 (CVSS 9.6), utilizes the default `local_trusted` mode to perform a DNS rebinding attack, hijacking developer local machine privileges. A Metasploit PoC attack module has emerged, but there are no reports of actual exploitation yet. The official team has patched the permission review mechanism in version v2026.416.0 and advises administrators to update promptly and review registration and deployment settings.",
