    category: "前瞻技術",
    title: "Black Hat 2026：多家主流 AI 瀏覽器仍難防間接 Prompt Injection 攻擊",
    summary: "Brave Software 安全工程師 Artem Chaikin 在 Black Hat USA 2026 發表研究指出，儘管多家廠商採用系統級提示詞、信任內容標籤與次級模型掃描，包含 Opera、Perplexity Comet 和 ChatGPT Atlas 等 AI 瀏覽器仍易受間接提示詞注入（Prompt Injection）攻擊。攻擊者可透過隱藏於 HTML、圖片疊加文字或 spoiler 標籤的惡意指令，騙過防護機制並導致資料外洩或帳號遭奪取。研究更發現 Atlas 的信任標籤可被偽造，且免費使用者因用量限制被降級模型時更容易被突破。專家指出，目前尚無完美的單一修補方案，應採取縱深防禦策略，如隔離瀏覽器設定檔、設置最低模型安全門檻、以及引入 Sentinel 次級驗證模型進行對齊檢查。",
    tags: ["Black Hat 2026", "Prompt Injection", "AI 瀏覽器", "Brave", "ChatGPT Atlas", "Opera", "Perplexity", "Agentic AI"],
    title_en: "Black Hat 2026: Multiple Major AI Browsers Still Vulnerable to Indirect Prompt Injection Attacks",
    summary_en: "Brave Software security engineer Artem Chaikin presented research at Black Hat USA 2026, indicating that despite multiple vendors implementing system-level prompts, trusted content labels, and secondary model scanning, AI browsers such as Opera, Perplexity Comet, and ChatGPT Atlas remain susceptible to indirect Prompt Injection attacks. Attackers can trick defense mechanisms and cause data leakage or account takeover by embedding malicious instructions within HTML, image overlays, or spoiler tags. The research also found that Atlas's trusted labels can be forged, and free users are more susceptible to breaches when downgraded to lower models due to usage limits. Experts point out that there is currently no perfect single patch, necessitating a defense-in-depth strategy, such as isolating browser profiles, setting minimum model security thresholds, and introducing a Sentinel secondary validation model for alignment checks.",
    tags_en: ["Black Hat 2026", "Prompt Injection", "AI Browsers", "Brave", "ChatGPT Atlas", "Opera", "Perplexity", "Agentic AI"],
