    title: "Google ADK for Python 爆代理間攻擊漏洞，駭客可利用提示詞注入威脅軟體供應鏈",
    summary: "Pillar Security 研究人員在 Google 的開源 ADK for Python（adk-python）中發現漏洞，成功展示首例生產環境中的「代理對代理（Agent-to-Agent）」攻擊。低特權且面向公眾的 AI 代理（如負責審查 GitHub PR 的 Agent）可被包含惡意提示詞注入的 PR 或 Issue 操縱，發送特定格式的命令並觸發高特權 AI 代理執行未授權操作，甚至在 CI/CD 流程中批准惡意程式碼。Google 已於 7 月完成修補。研究人員建議企業應檢視涉及代理的自動化流程，並限制 AI 代理權限與跨權限呼叫。",
    tags: ["Google", "Agent Development Kit", "AI Agent", "Prompt Injection", "軟體供應鏈安全", "Pillar Security", "Gemini"],
    title_en: "Vulnerability in Google ADK for Python Allows Agent-to-Agent Attack, Threatening Software Supply Chains via Prompt Injection",
    summary_en: "Researchers at Pillar Security discovered a vulnerability in Google's open-source ADK for Python (adk-python), successfully demonstrating the first instance of an 'Agent-to-Agent' attack in a production environment. Low-privilege, public-facing AI agents (such as those responsible for reviewing GitHub PRs) can be manipulated by malicious prompt injection within a PR or Issue, causing them to send specific formatted commands and triggering high-privilege AI agents to execute unauthorized operations, even approving malicious code within a CI/CD pipeline. Google completed the patch in July. Researchers recommend that enterprises review automated processes involving agents and restrict AI agent permissions and cross-privilege calls.",
